"Annual Report 2019","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/539404/5394040319.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2018","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/539404/5394040318.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2017","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/539404/5394040317.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2016","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/bseplus/AnnualReport/539404/5394040316.pdf","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2015","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/HIS_ANN_RPT/HISTANNR/2015/SATIN_CREDITCARE_NETWORK_LTD-539404-MARCH-2015.PDF","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2014","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/HIS_ANN_RPT/HISTANNR/2014/SATIN_CREDITCARE_NETWORK_LTD-539404-MARCH-2014.PDF","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2013","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/HIS_ANN_RPT/HISTANNR/2013/SATIN_CREDITCARE_NETWORK_LTD-539404-MARCH-2013.PDF","source":"bse"},{"kind":"annual_report","date":"","title":"Annual Report 2012","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/HIS_ANN_RPT/HISTANNR/2012/SATIN_CREDITCARE_NETWORK_LTD-539404-MARCH-2012.PDF","source":"bse"}],"analysis":{"summary":"Management reported a strong first quarter for FY27, highlighting 20 consecutive quarters of profitability, record first-quarter disbursements, and robust growth across consolidated and standalone metrics. The company increased its provision buffers and management overlays to remain cycle-proof despite potential rural monsoon risks and floods in Assam. Furthermore, management updated its guidance for FY27, maintaining targets for AUM growth, credit costs, and return on assets while executing a broader diversification strategy across its subsidiaries. Satin Creditcare Network Limited reported strong financial results for Q4 and FY26, with consolidated AUM crossing INR15,174 crores and consolidated PAT reaching INR330 crores for the full year. Management highlighted improvements in asset quality, a reduction in credit costs, and steady growth across its non-MFI subsidiaries like Satin Housing Finance and Satin Finserv.","themes":{"guidance":[{"claim":"The company guided for a consolidated AUM growth of 20% to 25% for FY27.","quote":"Guidance for FY27. Our guidance for FY27 is consolidated AUM growth of 20% to 25%, implying INR18,200 crores to INR18,900 crores by March '27.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Management guided for standalone credit costs of 3% to 3.5% on a reported basis for FY27.","quote":"Stand-alone credit cost of 3% to 3.5% on a reported basis.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The company guided for standalone AUM growth of 15% to 20% year-on-year for FY27.","quote":"For FY26-'27, our standalone guidance is AUM growth of 15% to 20% year-on-year, implying an AUM of approximately INR14,800 crores to INR15,100 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"The management set a credit cost target of 3% to 3.5% for FY27.","quote":"Credit cost target of 3% to 3.5%, a meaningful improvement from 3.8% in FY26.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"The company expects consolidated AUM growth to be closer to 25% to 30%.","quote":"Now keeping a mix of both that, if we add up to what 15%, that's the baseline which we are taking the bare minimum for microfinance, I think it will be closer to about 25%, 30% for a consolidated basis.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"Management noted that the revised monsoon outlook warrants caution on rural cash flows over the next two to three months.","quote":"Two things we are watching and we would rather name them. The revised monsoon outlook warrants caution on rural cash flows over the next 2 to 3 months.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Management stated that the West Asia situation has had no discernible impact on the business to date.","quote":"The West Asia situation has had no discernible impact on our business to date.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Management stated that the sector passed its stress peak by early 2026.","quote":"By early 2026, the sector had passed its stress peak.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"The company stated that there is currently no stress due to geopolitical crises in any of its operational states.","quote":"No right now there is no stress because of this geopolitical crisis across in any of our states or any of the places where we work upon.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"The company added 392 new branches in FY26.","quote":"We have 392 new branches added in FY26, a seasoned field team present in over 1 lakh villages and 550-plus districts, a robust ALM and a track record of 19 consecutive profitable quarters.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"Standalone net interest margin improved to 14.36% from 13.16% on a gross yield of 22.44% against a cost of funds of 8.08%.","quote":"On margins and efficiency, stand-alone NIM improved to 14.36% from 13.16% on gross yield of 22.44% against a cost of funds of 8.08%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The operating expense ratio improved to 6.33% from 6.98% in Q4.","quote":"Our operating expense ratio improved to 6.33% from 6.98% in Q4 as the 392 branches added last year begin to season.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Cost to income improved to 44.49% from 48.91% year-on-year.","quote":"Cost to income improved to 44.49% from 48.91% year-on-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The marginal cost of borrowing declined by 43 basis points to 10.82%.","quote":"Our marginal cost of borrowing declined 43 basis points to 10.82%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"Credit cost for FY26 stood at 3.8%, marking a 77 basis point improvement from FY25.","quote":"Our credit cost for FY '26 stood at 3.8%, a 77 basis point improvement from the 4.6% we recorded in FY '25.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"Consolidated AUM reached INR15,935 crores, growing 27% year-on-year and 5% sequentially.","quote":"Consolidated AUM reached INR15,935 crores, growing 27% year-on-year and 5% sequentially.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Standalone AUM stood at INR13,312 crores, up 22% year-on-year.","quote":"Stand-alone AUM stood at INR13,312 crores, up 22% year-on-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"X-bucket collection efficiency was 99.9% and every top state is at 99.6% or better.","quote":"X-bucket collection efficiency was 99.9% and every one of our top states is at 99.6% or better.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Consolidated AUM crossed INR15,174 crores, growing 19% year-on-year.","quote":"At a consolidated level, our AUM crossed INR15,174 crores, growing 19% year-on-year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"The standalone AUM stood at INR12,853 crores, up 14% year-on-year.","quote":"On a stand-alone basis, our AUM stood at INR12,853 crores, up 14% year-on-year, backed by disbursements of INR11,202 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"capital_allocation":[{"claim":"The company raised approximately INR3,000 crores during the quarter through diversified instruments including INR285 crores of subordinated debt.","quote":"We raised approximately INR3,000 crores during the quarter through diversified instruments, including INR285 crores of subordinated debt, which took our subordinated liabilities to INR497 crores and supported a capital adequacy ratio of 26.74%, up from 25.39% in March.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"Shareholders approved a promoter infusion of INR100 crores at approximately a 17% premium to the minimum issue price under SEBI regulation.","quote":"Shareholders have approved the promoter infusion of INR100 crores at approximately a 17% premium to the minimum issue price under SEBI regulation.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The company raised INR10,826 crores during FY26.","quote":"On funding, we raised INR10,826 crores during FY '26.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"},{"claim":"The company maintains a balance sheet liquidity of INR2,092 crores and undrawn sanction of INR2,235 crores.","quote":"We maintain a healthy balance sheet liquidity of INR2,092 crores and undrawn sanction of INR2,235 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}],"risks_headwinds":[{"claim":"The sector previously navigated headwinds including borrower overleveraging, state-level disruption, and a tightening of credit standards.","quote":"The sector navigated a confluence of headwinds, borrower overleveraging, state-level disruption and a tightening of credit standards across lenders.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf"}]},"management_commitments":[{"claim":"The company targets a non-MFI portfolio share of 30% by 2030.","quote":"On diversification, non-MFI portfolio now stands at 99 -- sorry, 19% of consolidated AUM against 14% a year ago and a target of 30% by 2030.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf","timeframe":"2030"},{"claim":"The core banking platform has completed development and moved into customer UAT with go-live targeted for Q2 FY27.","quote":"Our core banking platform has completed development and moved into customer UAT with go-live targeted for Q2 FY27, after which we expand into loan management and loan origination for NBFCs.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf","timeframe":"Q2 FY27"},{"claim":"The company revised its long-term consolidated AUM target for 2030 to INR32,000 crores.","quote":"As mentioned earlier, we are also revising our long-term AUM target upward from INR25,000 crores to INR32,000 crores by 2030 with a non-MFI AUM target of 30% by that date.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf","timeframe":"2030"},{"claim":"The company set a target for non-MFI AUM to reach 30% by 2030.","quote":"Our target is 30% by 2030.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-05-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=27c4ec79-dcea-408f-aef0-1eccc6e9e3cd.pdf","timeframe":"2030"}],"coverage":{"docs_analysed":3,"kinds":["concall_transcript","concall_ppt"]}},"_meta":{"model":"gemini-3.6-flash","grounded":true,"facts_kept":29,"facts_dropped_ungrounded":5,"note":"Facts are verbatim-grounded against the company's own documents; claims whose quote was not found were dropped."}}